This product's design is informed by the Astral `uv` project
(https://github.com/astral-sh/uv), specifically the uv-resolver crate's
approach to adapting a generic version solver to Python packaging semantics
(candidate selection, extras as virtual packages, and the separation between
the solver core and metadata retrieval). uv is dual-licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0, or the MIT license.

The PubGrub algorithm this module drives is described by Natalie Weizenbaum
(https://medium.com/@nex3/pubgrub-2fb6470504f) and in the Dart `pub` package
manager's solver documentation (https://github.com/dart-lang/pub), by Natalie
Weizenbaum and the Dart team.

konstin's Rust implementations of PEP 440 and PEP 508 informed the PEP
primitives this module consumes from github.com/posit-dev/go-python-packaging.

The pypirsf/ package's PyPI record layout and dependency-blob decoder are ported
from Posit Package Manager (rstudio/package-manager), specifically src/rsf/types
and src/rsf/depsblob, Copyright (c) Posit Software, PBC, contributed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0, or the MIT license. The decode side only is
ported; the encoder remains in the producer pipeline. The golden test vectors
in pypirsf/testdata originate from that producer's own test fixtures, so they
pin this decoder to the encoder rather than only to itself.

index/testdata/pypi-trimmed.rsf is an excerpt of a Repository Snapshot Format
file produced by Posit Package Manager's PyPI manifest tooling, Copyright (c)
Posit Software, PBC. Its records are copied byte for byte, so it also carries
that producer's trained compression dictionary. The metadata within — project
names, versions, Requires-Dist, Requires-Python, Provides-Extra and release
summaries — originates with the projects published on the Python Package Index.
The excerpt is included so that tests read what the producer emits rather than
what this module's own writer emits; see index/testdata/README.md for its
composition and how it was derived.

